[{:adr/consequences "{:shared_engine_different_layers \"net-babiniku and network-isekai both render VRM via the\\n                                    same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, through\\n                                    different integration layers fit to each app's own\\n                                    stack/audience\", :sdk_validation \"validates kami-engine-sdk's webvr + pluggable-onScene design as reusable\\n                   across two unrelated domains (incident-response drills, AI-companion\\n                   roleplay)\", :new_backend_needed \"standalone backend (LLM chat + TTS + governor) and private data\\n                       store to build; nothing inherited automatically from\\n                       network-isekai's backend/\", :scaffold_shape_followup \"network-isekai-like scaffold (README + 90-docs/adr +\\n                            package.json, ADR-driven), not ai-gftd-isekai's dodaf\\n                            PROJECT.jsonld/OWNERS/nanoid shape -- net-babiniku is a\\n                            kami-engine app in network-isekai's lineage, not part of the\\n                            ai-gftd-*/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp product-registry line\", :out_of_scope_followup \"exact LLM provider(s), pricing/currency model, and detailed\\n                          moderation policy are product decisions out of scope for this\\n                          architecture ADR\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["gftdcojp/net-babiniku is a NEW, separate repo from gftdcojp/network-isekai -- both\n    render VRM avatars via the same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, but through\n    different integration layers (Svelte + @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk for net-babiniku vs\n    hand-rolled ClojureScript/reagent glue for network-isekai) and for different audiences\n    (private single-purpose AI-companion product vs open public forkable game platform)" "net-babiniku's product shape is modeled on isekaizero.ai (interactive AI stories,\n    choices-matter roleplay chat, per-character voice) but replaces its 2D visual-novel\n    character portraits with a live-rendered 3D VRM avatar (VTuber presentation), via\n    kami-engine-sdk's VrmViewer/createVrmEngine" "net-babiniku reuses kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner\n    (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph, pluggable onScene renderer) --\n    originally built for cyber-drill's incident-response drills -- repurposed to\n    conversational roleplay content, supplying VrmViewer as the onScene renderer instead\n    of cyber-drill's vendor-private three.js scene" "AI-persona content is containment + governor per the existing Actors doctrine: the\n    LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue, emotion, motion-cue} only; a separate\n    ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is spoken via\n    TTS; every commit/hold is appended to an audit ledger" "net-babiniku's data model is private/per-user (chat sessions, personas, avatar\n    customization), NOT network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN\n    model -- kotoba-style content-addressing may still be used internally for asset\n    caching only"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.md" "90-docs/adr/2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation.md"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607051800-net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber-design", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/amendments "[{:date \"2026-07-05\", :what \"frontend stack corrected to ClojureScript + reagent/re-frame + kami-webgpu +\\n          kotoba-lang/vrm, matching network-isekai's own toolchain exactly -- per direct\\n          user direction, superseding the :frontend and :turn_engine decisions above\\n          (Svelte 5 + @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk + webvr's headless choice-scenario\\n          runner)\", :unchanged [\"the :ai_persona_containment decision (LLM-persona proposes only, a\\n                separate governor is the sole path to a renderable/speakable turn,\\n                append-only ledger) -- re-expressed in .cljc (babiniku.governor/\\n                review-turn) instead of TypeScript, gated by `nbb governor`\" \"the :data_model decision (private, per-user)\"], :retires [\"alternative #3 (reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer) -- moot, no\\n              webvr/SDK dependency left to supply an onScene renderer for\"], :deployed \"Milestone 0 placeholder: a kami-webgpu render loop (placeholder box by\\n              default, real live VRM avatar via ?vrm=<url> through babiniku.vrm-bridge,\\n              adapted from isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc) + reagent/re-frame UI with a live\\n              governor demo, on Cloudflare Pages -- https://net-babiniku.pages.dev. No\\n              LLM backend, no TTS, no real chat yet.\"}]", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-05", :adr/decision "{:repo {:org \"gftdcojp\", :visibility :private, :rationale \"human-centric/business scope per repos.edn :orgs; gftdcojp default\\n                     visibility is private per repos.edn :orgs :visibility (ADR-2607021330)\", :registration \"plain-git child repo, manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects ->\\n                        manifest/west.yml, --entry net-babiniku minimal-diff generation\"}, :frontend {:stack \"Svelte 5 via @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk (VrmViewer/createVrmEngine), NOT\\n           network-isekai's ClojureScript/reagent\", :rationale \"the SDK already packages the live-avatar render surface (wgpu/WASM,\\n               three.js-free); network-isekai's isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc/isekai.stage.cljc\\n               predate the SDK and hand-roll the same glue directly against kami-web wasm\\n               -- no reason to redo that work in CLJS for a second app\"}, :turn_engine {:what \"kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner\\n          (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph), repurposed from\\n          incident-response drill content to conversational-roleplay content\", :renderer \"VrmViewer supplied as the onScene callback -- net-babiniku is webvr's\\n              SECOND consumer (after cyber-drill) and FIRST VrmViewer-as-onScene consumer,\\n              validating the headless-engine/pluggable-renderer split across two\\n              unrelated domains\"}, :expression_motion {:model \"each LLM turn emits {dialogue emotion motion-cue}; emotion drives the SDK's\\n           morph builder (facial blend-shape targets), motion-cue drives the bone/motion\\n           builder (idle/gesture pose) -- data-driven render state, same philosophy as\\n           kami.dance's pose-from-EDN but keyed to conversation turns instead of a beat\\n           grid\"}, :voice {:what \"SDK's voice builder drives per-character TTS, matching isekaizero.ai's\\n          per-character-voice Visual Novel Mode but spoken through a live avatar\", :backend \"net-babiniku stands up its OWN backend (LLM chat completion + TTS) --\\n             independent deploy from network-isekai's backend/ (Modal GPU: TRELLIS/\\n             image/TTS/music); where the same Modal-GPU-TTS pattern applies, copy-adapt\\n             rather than cross-repo depend, matching isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc's own\\n             precedent for character-creator's gpu-adapter\"}, :ai_persona_containment {:pattern \"Actors doctrine (CLAUDE.md Actors section; precedent isekai.moderation.cljc):\\n             LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue emotion motion-cue} only; a separate\\n             ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is\\n             spoken via TTS; every commit/hold appended to an audit ledger\", :non_negotiable true}, :data_model {:what \"private, per-user chat sessions / personas / avatar customization -- NOT\\n          network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN model\", :kotoba_use \"content-addressing may still be used internally for asset caching\\n                (avatar/voice asset dedup) only -- no public asset hub, no fork-by-URL\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-05: design gftdcojp/net-babiniku, separate from\\n           gftdcojp/network-isekai, sharing the same kami engine, shaped as a VRM/VTuber\\n           app in the spirit of isekaizero.ai\", :investigated [\"isekaizero.ai (ISEKAI ZERO, ARX MEDIA SDN BHD): interactive AI story/roleplay mobile\\n    app, #1 Games/#2 Entertainment App Store (2026-05), chat with LLM characters +\\n    choices-matter narrative + experimental Visual Novel Mode (2D background/character\\n    images with expression/pose swaps + per-character TTS), multi-LLM backend\\n    (Deepseek 3.2 default, switchable Gemini/Grok), Mana(free)/Arcane(paid) dual currency\" \"network-isekai is an open 'CodePen for games' platform: games + VRM :dance stages\\n    (kami.dance/kami-live vocabulary, isekai.stage.cljc + isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc hand-rolled\\n    against kami-web wasm directly) + asset hub, everything public/forkable EDN in Datomic\\n    via kotoba -- VRM is one mode among several, not the product's identity, and the\\n    public/forkable data model is wrong for private AI-companion chat sessions\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk (@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk, Svelte 5, three.js-free per\\n    ADR-2605264300) already packages VrmViewer/createVrmEngine (live VRM avatar via\\n    Rust+wgpu WASM KamiWasmExports, no three.js) + headless morph/bone/motion/voice/\\n    emotion builders + `./webvr` (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph,\\n    pluggable onScene renderer) -- built after network-isekai's own vrm-bridge glue, for\\n    exactly this kind of app\" \"no existing product combines webvr's choice engine with VrmViewer as the onScene\\n    renderer; cyber-drill (the only current webvr consumer) supplies its own vendor-private\\n    three.js renderer for incident-response drills, an unrelated domain\" \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai checked and is unrelated -- a Minecraft-voxel-sandbox x\\n    creature-collection game (isekai.gftd.ai) sharing kami-engine's WebGPU renderer and the\\n    'isekai' name only coincidentally\"], :risk \"AI-companion/roleplay chat is a known content-moderation surface; 'babiniku'\\n         (バ美肉, embodying a VRM/VTuber persona) framing raises the stakes of getting the\\n         containment/governor boundary right from the start, not as a retrofit.\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"build it as a new mode/page inside network-isekai (like assets.html/\\n            generate.html today)\", :rejected_because \"different audience (private product vs open platform) and different\\n                       data model (private chat sessions vs public forkable EDN) --\\n                       architecturally wrong, not a styling difference; would also keep\\n                       the ClojureScript/re-frame stack instead of the SDK's native Svelte\\n                       packaging\"} {:option \"reimplement VRM rendering glue directly (network-isekai's own\\n            isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc + isekai.stage.cljc pattern) instead of depending on\\n            kami-engine-sdk\", :rejected_because \"the SDK already packages VrmViewer + morph/bone/voice/emotion\\n                       builders for exactly this; redoing it in CLJS+JS glue duplicates\\n                       real, already-built work for no benefit\"} {:option \"reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer as the webvr onScene\\n            implementation\", :rejected_because \"cyber-drill's renderer is vendor-private and three.js-based; the SDK\\n                       is explicitly three.js-free (ADR-2605264300) and VrmViewer's native\\n                       wgpu path is the better-fit, on-brand renderer for a VTuber avatar\\n                       body\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607051800: net-babiniku -- a new gftdcojp product, AI VTuber/VRM companion\n          chat, distinct from network-isekai but sharing the kami engine"}]